{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(ii): record trip TRP-00201 as a false-arrival event against driver DRV-01590, no qualifying in-geofence fix existing anywhere in the trip."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "The $4.00 no-show cancellation fee charged for trip TRP-00201 does not stand. It is refunded to the rider in full, and no driver compensation is payable.\n\nWhy, on the driver's own evidence: EV-GPS-00201 (weight 1.0, 100% coverage, 10-second sampling, 98 fixes across the whole window) places the driver no closer than 779.93 m from the pickup pin at Blk 118 Rivervale Drive, with a mean distance of 1,177.11 m. The STANDARD arrival radius is 50 m, so there is not one qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere in the trip. Under POL-NS-02 the driver never arrived and POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails. Limb (c) fails independently: the longest qualifying in-geofence run is 0 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum. With (b) and (c) gone, the $4.00 fee is not chargeable under POL-NS-01, and it is refunded under POL-NS-06 as well (effective in-geofence dwell 0 seconds, short of the 300-second minimum).\n\nThe trip record's 'arrived' event at 08:02:14 (EV-TRIP-00201) does not rescue the charge. Under POL-NS-05 a marker set when the trace puts the driver more than 300 m from the pin is FALSE; every one of the 98 fixes is 779.93 m or further out, so the marker is false and does not start the waiting clock. Recomputed from the first qualifying in-geofence fix there is none, so POL-NS-05(ii) applies: full refund, no compensation, and the trip is recorded against the driver as a false-arrival event (see referrals).\n\nIndependently, POL-NS-04 is satisfied: the rider sent a locating message ('hello? i dont see any car at 118') at 08:05:33, the driver neither replied within 120 seconds nor made any in-app call before terminating at 08:09:40, and the rider's device stayed within 24.93 m of the pin across all 122 fixes, far inside the 100 m STANDARD presence radius. That clause also yields a full refund with no driver compensation.\n\nThe driver's argument that POL-NS-09(b) requires a human escalation is not accepted. Limb (b) fires only where two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence 'and no clause resolves the conflict'. Here POL-NS-05 is the clause that resolves it: it declares the arrived marker false and recomputes the waiting clock from the geofence test, which is exactly what POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-01(b) make the definitive measure of arrival. There is therefore no unresolved contradiction, and the case is decided now rather than held. The other escalation limbs are also clear: no POL-NS-08 impairment attaches to the deciding artifacts (the 08:02:14 arrival event falls inside the trace window and both records agree the trip terminated at 08:09:40; the trace has no gaps, 98 fixes and the rider track present; the chat log's 2 messages match trip_record.chat_message_count of 2; and the $4.00 fee reconciles with the fee schedule), both parties' disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0, the driver's no_show_terminations_30d is 3 against 96 completed trips (3.1%), and the rider's no_show_disputes_30d is 0. The remaining profile numbers (rating, cancellation_rate, lifetime_trips, prior_disputes_upheld, prior_no_show_flags) are context only under POL-GEN-01 and carry no finding.\n\nPOL-NS-03 (wrong entrance / pin ambiguity) does not apply: that clause is limited to a driver stationary within 400 m of the pin, and the driver's closest approach was 779.93 m, roughly twice the ceiling. No refund allocation under POL-NS-03 and no 50 percent pin-ambiguity goodwill arise, and the driver claims neither.\n\nFigures used, from the money block: one cancellation fee of $4.00 (EV-FARE-00201), being the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee ($4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee ($4.00), charged and not refunded (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). The ruling moves SGD 4.00, returning the whole contested amount to the filing rider."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "None of the POL-NS-09 escalation triggers is engaged, so this case should be decided now with a full refund rather than put on hold. The anti-farming check reads driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d = 3 against driver_profile.completed_trips_30d = 96, i.e. 3.1%, below both the 4-termination and 0.08 thresholds in POL-NS-07, so limb (d) does not fire; rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0 and both parties' disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0, so limb (c) does not fire; no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence; and the deciding facts rest on artifacts at weight 1.0, the only sub-1.0 artifact being the MISSING advisory at 0.0 on which no positive fact rests. Under POL-NS-09 the disputed fee is held only if a trigger fires, and none does; POL-GEN-02 caps confidence at the weight of the artifacts carrying the deciding fact, which is 1.0.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00201-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
